posts.text:
In a lecture I gave last year (https://t.co/gyBq2vRbvD), I shared a mental model for AI: the convex hull of humanity’s collective knowledge.

Human expertise is highly specialized and fragmented across people and fields. I hypothesized that there might be a huge overhang of new knowledge accessible through “interpolation”: connecting the dots in this high-dimensional knowledge space.

@_jasonwei  and the team are showing what connecting the dots can look like with an existing trove of health data. Exciting to see AI helping researchers turn that data into new scientific insights!

posts.translationZh:
在去年的一次演讲中（https://t.co/gyBq2vRbvD），我分享了一个理解 AI 的思维模型：人类集体知识的凸包。

人类的专业知识高度专门化，分散在不同的人和领域中。我当时提出，通过“插值”，也就是在这个高维知识空间中建立联系，或许能挖掘出大量尚未被发现的新知识。

@_jasonwei 和团队正利用现有的海量健康数据，展示这种融会贯通能带来什么。很高兴看到 AI 帮助研究人员将这些数据转化为新的科学洞见！

